-- Optional: update unchanged default bios without overwriting admin edits.
-- Back up the database before applying this script.
SET NAMES utf8mb4;
START TRANSACTION;
UPDATE `team_members` SET `bio` = 'রোশন তাইয়িন মেক্সা মোশনের প্রতিষ্ঠাতা ও লিড মেন্টর। ভিডিও এডিটিং, স্টোরিটেলিং এবং টিম পরিচালনার অভিজ্ঞতা নিয়ে তিনি স্টুডিওর সৃজনশীল কাজের দিকনির্দেশনা দেন। বাংলাদেশের ইনফরমেটিক কনটেন্টের ধরন বদলে দেওয়ার কাজে তিনি Voice of Dhaka এর সঙ্গে যুক্ত ছিলেন। দেশের বিভিন্ন শীর্ষ চ্যানেলের এডিটিং টিমের সঙ্গে কাজ করার অভিজ্ঞতাও তাঁর রয়েছে। নিজের হাতে তৈরি করা ভিডিও আন্তর্জাতিক মার্কেটপ্লেসে দর্শকের কাছে পৌঁছেছে।\n\nপ্রতিটি প্রজেক্টের শুরুতে তিনি ক্লায়েন্টের ভাবনা, কাজের উদ্দেশ্য ও সময়সীমা বোঝার ওপর গুরুত্ব দেন। এরপর ফুটেজ থেকে গল্পের মূল বিষয়টি খুঁজে বের করে সেটিকে পরিপাটি ও সহজবোধ্য উপস্থাপনায় রূপ দিতে টিমকে সহায়তা করেন। তাঁর কাজের মধ্যে এডিটিংয়ের গতি, গল্পের ধারাবাহিকতা এবং ব্র্যান্ডের পরিচয় বজায় রাখার বিষয়গুলো বিশেষ গুরুত্ব পায়।\n\nস্টুডিওতে রোশন প্রজেক্টের চূড়ান্ত মান যাচাই করেন এবং নতুন সদস্যদের কাজ শেখাতে ও উন্নত করতে মেন্টরিং করেন। ক্লায়েন্টের ব্রিফ থেকে ফাইনাল ডেলিভারি পর্যন্ত সবার মধ্যে পরিষ্কার যোগাযোগ বজায় রাখাও তাঁর ভূমিকার অংশ। Premiere Pro, সৃজনশীল পরিকল্পনা এবং পোস্ট প্রোডাকশন স্ট্র্যাটেজি তাঁর কাজের পরিচিত ক্ষেত্র। তাঁর লক্ষ্য হলো প্রতিটি ভিডিওতে ক্লায়েন্টের ভাবনাকে সম্মান করে এমন একটি ফলাফল তৈরি করা, যা গল্পকে স্পষ্টভাবে তুলে ধরে এবং টিমের সবার সম্মিলিত দক্ষতার প্রতিফলন ঘটায়।' WHERE `slug` = 'rowshan-taieen' AND BINARY `bio` = BINARY 'বাংলাদেশের ইনফরমেটিক কন্টেন্ট এর পুরো প্যাটার্ন পাল্টে দিয়েছি আমি Voice of Dhaka এর হাত ধরে। সাথে বাংলাদেশের টপ সব চ্যানেলে এডিটিং করে যাচ্ছি আর নিজের হাতে তৈরি করা বড় ভিডিও ইন্টারন্যাশনাল মার্কেটপ্লেসে নিজেদের আলাদা জায়গা করে নিয়েছে।';
UPDATE `team_members` SET `description` = 'Arif Hossain is a Dhaka-based senior video editor who brings seven years of timeline experience to Mexa Motion. Much of his work has focused on long-form videos for YouTube creators and course sellers, where a clear story and a thoughtful pace matter as much as a polished finish. He starts with the raw footage, identifies the strongest ideas and builds an edit that gives viewers a clear opening, a natural progression and an ending that feels complete.\n\nArif works in Premiere Pro and pays close attention to dialogue, rhythm and the moments that keep an audience engaged. Rather than cutting simply to make a video shorter, he looks for ways to preserve the creator\'s meaning while removing distractions. His experience also includes audio cleanup and caption styling, helping the wider team prepare a consistent handoff for colour and sound.\n\nAt the studio, Arif leads the first cut and story pass on long-form projects. He reviews editor drafts before they reach clients, keeps project files and export names organised, and mentors junior editors on retention-focused pacing. His approach combines careful listening with practical organisation, so each project can move through the production process with a clear creative direction and a reliable foundation for the final edit.' WHERE `slug` = 'arif-hossain' AND BINARY `description` = BINARY 'Dhaka-based editor with seven years behind the timeline, most of them spent cutting long-form for YouTube creators and course sellers. Arif takes raw footage and builds a story with a clear opening, a pace that holds attention past the ten-minute mark and an ending that lands, then hands the cut to colour and sound with clean, labelled project files. His strengths are story structure, pacing and dialogue-driven editing in Premiere Pro. Inside the studio he leads the first cut on every long-form project and mentors the junior editors on retention-focused pacing.';
UPDATE `team_members` SET `description` = 'Nusrat Jahan is a YouTube editor who helps creator channels move from recorded footage to a finished upload. She is a regular point of contact for clients and coordinates the weekly delivery cycle, bringing editing and workflow planning together. Her work often involves shaping long interviews into clear, watchable chapters while preserving the tone and personality of the creator.\n\nIn Premiere Pro, Nusrat trims dead air, selects useful moments and styles captions so viewers can follow the story. She reads rough transcripts to find strong sections and prepares chapter markers and caption files as part of the delivery. Her approach is practical and detail-oriented: an edit should feel natural, make the important points easy to follow and be ready for its scheduled publishing time.\n\nWithin Mexa Motion, Nusrat coordinates the publishing calendar with clients and helps the team keep weekly uploads on track. She also flags missing footage before editing begins, giving everyone time to address gaps in the brief. Alongside interview editing and caption styling, her skills include choosing thumbnail stills and planning the work needed for each release. By balancing clear communication with careful editing, she helps creators maintain a consistent workflow without losing the individual voice that makes their content recognisable.' WHERE `slug` = 'nusrat-jahan' AND BINARY `description` = BINARY 'Nusrat is the editor most clients talk to every week. She runs the upload cycle for creator channels — turning long interviews into watchable chapters, styling captions, cutting dead air and making sure each video is finished before the scheduled publish time without sanding off the creator\'s own tone. She works fast in Premiere Pro and is unusually good at reading a rough transcript to find the best twenty seconds. In the team she owns weekly delivery and coordinates the publish calendar with clients.';
UPDATE `team_members` SET `description` = 'Tanvir Ahmed is a motion graphics designer who gives video edits their animated visual layer. With five years of After Effects experience across brand films, advertisements and creator channels, he works on elements that make information easier to follow while supporting the story. His projects include logo reveals, lower thirds, transitions and animated callouts, all designed around the type and colour system of the client.\n\nTanvir\'s strengths include vector animation, kinetic typography and clean transitions. He pays attention to the balance between movement and clarity, so a graphic can add emphasis without taking attention away from the content. Whether an editor needs an introduction or a small detail inside a longer video, he works to make the animation feel consistent with the surrounding footage and the brand\'s visual identity.\n\nAt Mexa Motion, Tanvir maintains the shared motion template library and creates reusable assets that editors can bring into their projects. He also prepares alpha-channel exports when an animation needs to be placed over other footage. This organised approach helps the team keep visual elements on brand across different edits. By combining technical preparation with thoughtful design, he supports a smoother handoff between motion graphics and editing, from the first creative idea through to the finished video.' WHERE `slug` = 'tanvir-ahmed' AND BINARY `description` = BINARY 'Tanvir brings five years of After Effects work across brand films, ads and creator channels. He designs the animated layer of a video: logo reveals, lower thirds, stat callouts, transitions and the small motion details that make an edit feel expensive, all built around the client\'s type and colour system. His strengths are vector animation, kinetic type and clean transitions that never distract from the story. He owns the studio\'s motion template library, so every editor can drop in an intro that already looks on brand.';
UPDATE `team_members` SET `description` = 'Sadia Islam is a thumbnail designer with a graphic design background and four years of experience creating YouTube thumbnails. She focuses on the frame that introduces a video to its audience, developing a clear visual idea that connects with the title and the content. Her work brings together composition, contrast, typography and carefully selected facial expressions to make the message readable at a glance.\n\nWorking in Photoshop, Sadia uses type hierarchy and face cut-outs to build thumbnails that are clear without becoming visually crowded. She pays attention to how an image will appear at smaller sizes and how each design fits alongside the other videos on a channel. Her aim is to give a creator a recognisable visual style while making the subject of each video easy to understand.\n\nFor each concept, Sadia prepares two variants so clients can compare different approaches. She considers the promise made by the thumbnail and makes sure it remains connected to the video itself. At Mexa Motion, she helps maintain visual consistency across channels and delivers platform-ready 1280 by 720 pixel exports in PNG and JPG formats. Her process combines a strong central idea with practical attention to layout, readability and the needs of the creator.' WHERE `slug` = 'sadia-islam' AND BINARY `description` = BINARY 'Sadia designs the frame that decides whether a video gets watched at all. From a graphic design background with four years of YouTube thumbnails, she works one clear idea per image: high contrast, short readable type and a face expression that matches the promise of the title — always in two variants so clients can test the click. Her toolkit is Photoshop, composition and type hierarchy. She keeps every channel\'s thumbnails visually consistent and delivers platform-ready 1280×720 exports.';
UPDATE `team_members` SET `description` = 'Rakib Hasan is a colourist and sound designer responsible for the finishing pass at Mexa Motion. With six years of grading and mixing experience, he works on the details that help a video look and sound consistent before delivery. His focus includes natural skin tones, balanced exposure between shots, clean dialogue and music that supports the voice rather than competing with it.\n\nRakib grades in DaVinci Resolve and considers how each shot relates to the rest of the edit. He looks for differences in exposure and colour that might distract from the story, then brings the footage together into a cohesive visual presentation. On the audio side, he cleans dialogue, manages room tone and balances music beds so the important words remain clear.\n\nHis work also includes checking loudness for the intended platforms and preparing final export settings. Because viewers may watch on everything from phones to larger screens, he pays attention to how the finished mix translates to everyday listening. At the studio, Rakib brings picture and sound together during the final stage, helping ensure that the creative decisions made earlier in the edit carry through to delivery. His approach is centred on clarity, consistency and a polished result that serves the content.' WHERE `slug` = 'rakib-hasan' AND BINARY `description` = BINARY 'Rakib is the last person to touch a project before it ships. With six years of grading and mixing, he fixes skin tones, balances exposure between shots, cleans dialogue down to the room tone and sits the music under the voice so nothing fights. He grades in DaVinci Resolve, mixes to platform loudness standards and prepares the final export settings. In the studio he owns the finishing pass, so every delivery leaves with a consistent look and a mix that survives phone speakers.';
UPDATE `team_members` SET `description` = 'Mim Akter is a Shorts and Reels editor who focuses on the vertical side of Mexa Motion\'s work. She began as a creator editing her own Reels and now edits short-form content for brands and creators. Her experience includes turning long-form material and raw footage into compact videos designed for platforms such as YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels and TikTok.\n\nMim pays particular attention to the opening moments of a video, exploring hooks that give viewers a reason to keep watching. She combines vertical framing, beat-matched cuts and readable on-screen captions to make each piece clear on a small screen. She also considers safe margins so important text and visuals are not hidden by platform interfaces.\n\nWithin the team, Mim owns short-form delivery and tests hook variants before a final version goes out. She keeps caption styles consistent for each client while adapting the edit to the needs of the footage and the intended platform. Her delivery work includes 9:16, 1:1 and 16:9 versions where needed. By bringing together pacing, framing and practical export preparation, she helps creators turn their material into short videos that stay true to their message and are ready to share.' WHERE `slug` = 'mim-akter' AND BINARY `description` = BINARY 'Mim cuts the vertical side of the studio. She started as a creator editing her own Reels and now cuts Shorts, Reels and TikToks for brands and creators full time — hooks in the first two seconds, beat-matched cuts, captions that stay readable on a small screen and safe margins so nothing hides under the app UI. She is fast with vertical framing, hook variants and caption styling. She owns short-form delivery in the team and tests hooks before anything goes out.';
COMMIT;
